  "foaf:name": "China Oceanic Development Foundation",
  "sdo:name": "China Oceanic Development Foundation",
  "sdo:description": "With a vision of &quot;The science we need for the ocean we want&quot;, the Ocean Decade aims to catalyze transformative scientific solutions that promote sustainable development and connect people and the oceans. Under the framework of the Ocean Decade, CODF is willing to take an active part in the organization, service and coordination of the Program, and establish close cooperation in market, technology, information and culture with the ocean. Through the scientific and technological innovation and the participation in multilateral ocean governance, CODF will continue to work with international society to encourage more research findings to be transformed into solutions, governance tools and public service products, and eventually make new contributions and open up new prospects for building a harmonious and bright future for the mankind. 1. Performing a good work of top-level design, actively initiating and participating in international cooperation organizations and plans. CODF will actively initiate or participate in major international cooperation organizations or plans and initiate or participate in the Ocean Decade Program with the help of international cooperation organizations or plans. Meanwhile, CODF will work with the Authority for marine affaires of China and formulate more flexible and effective policies and measures to promote the international cooperation among national and international organizations, to provide impetus for China&#x27;s deep participation in global ocean governance and the building of a maritime community with a shared future. 2. Building the bridge for international cooperation, seeking partners and advocacy action plan. With the help of international cooperation platform such as Ocean Decade, CODF will attract partners from China to jointly implement the action plan for Ocean Decade. CODF will promote the concept of building blue partnership and building a maritime community with a shared future to jointly build a harmonious ocean and promote the ocean sustainable development. 3. Multi-stakeholder Response to Ocean Decade. CODF has a close relationship with the government department (such as the Ministry of Natural Resources and the Ministry of Ecological Environment), national and local NGOs, Universities, etc. Thus, CODF can make full use of the Chinese research advantages and development basis to put forward diversified action plans. 4. Deepening strong involvement in building a maritime community with a shared future. A maritime community with a shared future is China&#x27;s plan to jointly safeguard the marine ecology, peace, order and prosperity. It focuses on answering the questions of &quot;how can mankind live in harmony with the ocean&quot; and &quot;how can mankind cooperate in the maritime field&quot;. In terms of connotation, both Ocean Decade and a maritime community with a shared future embody the concept of harmonious coexistence between man and nature and the ocean, as well as the concept of sustainable development.",
  "sdo:location": "China",
  "sdo:identifier": "828",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/china-oceanic-development-foundation/",
